.TH PRIVATE-VMD 8 "2026-07-19" "private-vm 0.0.0-dev" "System Administration"
.SH NAME
private-vmd \- privileged private-vm lifecycle daemon
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B private-vmd
[--config PATH] [--group GROUP]
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B private-vmd
runs as root and exposes only the bounded semantic gRPC API on
.IR /run/private-vm/control.sock .
It is not a generic command, mount, device or QEMU-argument service.
.PP
The systemd service owns startup, shutdown and recovery. Do not run multiple
instances and do not manually delete session resources before cleanup audits
them.
.SH SECURITY
The configuration file must contain no VPN key, magnet, password or token.
Core dumps are disabled. QMP and SPICE use private Unix sockets; guest RPC uses
AF_VSOCK. No daemon endpoint listens on TCP.
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR private-vm (1),
https://github.com/StevenBuglione/private-vm/blob/main/docs/28-operations-runbook.md
